    category: "ai-drug-discovery",
    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-10, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (111 hits across 27 query families, scan regenerated 2026-11-10 06:05 KST via 'bash run.sh scan', collected_at 2026-11-09T21:03 UTC). The score-9 band produced two genuinely NOVEL fresh accessions today (GSE353663 pdat 2026/11/08 and GSE305509 pdat 2026/11/08) alongside the long-recycled ladder (GSE328275 TNBC CD45 immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential lymph-node metastasis, GSE326553 opioid-dependence spatial, GSE346380 lung and GSE348495 colorectal CosMx resources, GSE288340 post-CAR-T marrow atlas, GSE311507 HNSCC dependency map, GSE281462/63/64/65 3D-chromatin-GWAS bundle and GSE353356 foregut morphogenesis), so for the second consecutive cycle the actionable harvest came from the score-9 tier itself rather than from the score-6/4 fallback band. Novelty was verified at two levels: an archive-wide accession check (git log --all -S <GSE> -- src/app/digest/page.tsx returned empty for GSE353663, GSE305509 and GSE349653) and a subject-level keyword cross-check confirming that the biological SUBJECTS of all three signals - Hippo-pathway-state reconstruction with an alphaV integrin vulnerability, DBI as a microglia-derived driver of glioma-related refractory epilepsy, and an isotype-intrinsic IgD avidity mechanism in lung-cancer plasma cells - have never been featured under any accession in any prior digest commit. All three records were verified against their live NCBI GEO esummary entries (title, depositor summary, taxon, sample count, pdat, gds_type) rather than by title matching alone. Signal 1 is GSE353663 (Homo sapiens, score 9, n=6, pdat 2026/11/08, raw CSV): StateMap is a framework that reconstructs pathway states by integrating CRISPR fitness dependencies with the transcriptional programs associated with them, and applied to the Hippo pathway it resolves a continuum of pathway activity into five interpretable regions that refine the conventional YAP-on/YAP-off binary - the commercially sharpest finding is the Hippo-strong state, defined by strong growth-restrictive effects of Hippo pathway genes DESPITE active YAP/TAZ signalling, in which cells selectively depend on integrin alphaVbeta5, ITGAV depletion induces Hippo-dependent cell aggregation followed by G1 arrest, projection onto tumour transcriptomes nominates a corresponding subset with elevated ITGB1/NNMT expression, and drug-response datasets plus validation assays show increased sensitivity of Hippo-strong models to the alphaV integrin inhibitor cilengitide. Signal 2 is GSE305509 (Homo sapiens, score 9, n=15, pdat 2026/11/08, raw TAR): in glioma-related drug-resistant epilepsy (40-90% of glioma patients depending on grade, one third of epilepsy patients refractory to anti-seizure medication), matched perifocal versus focal tissue profiling by Nanostring, scRNA-seq and high-dimensional immunofluorescence multiplexing of n=15 patients identified a unique microglia polarization state with elevated diazepam binding inhibitor (DBI, log2 FC 1.45), ex vivo human tissue culture confirmed higher DBI secretion from epileptogenic foci (85.72 ng/ml versus 55.67 ng/ml, P < 0.0001), Visium HD single-cell spatial transcriptomics on minimal-residual-disease glioblastoma samples (n=4) combined with scRNA-seq (n=110) showed robust DBI expression correlating with glioblastoma progression and tumour connectivity scores, and the authors built a first-in-class lipid-conjugate siRNA therapeutic (Ntx-DBI) that reduced mortality after intrathecal administration in epilepsy models. Signal 3 is GSE349653 (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=12, pdat 2026/11/08, raw TAR + CSV): a rare population of IgD-secreting plasma cells in non-small cell lung cancer shows extensive somatic hypermutation, clonal expansion and germinal-centre-dependent lineage relationships, and patient-derived monoclonal antibodies displayed markedly greater tumour-cell binding when expressed as IgD Fab2 than as IgG1 or IgM with identical variable regions - with monomeric IgD showing no enhanced mono- or bivalent binding kinetics, the mechanism is isotype-structural rather than sequence-derived: the IgD Fab2 region promotes reversible tetramers with potential octavalency, increasing avidity and polyreactivity.",
