    category: "longevity",
    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-07, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (112 hits across 27 query families, scan regenerated 2026-11-07 06:03 KST via 'bash run.sh scan', hits.jsonl mtime 2026-11-07 06:03, collected_at 2026-11-06T21:01 UTC). The score-9 band was once again fully recycled - the same long-standing top ladder (TNBC CD45+ immune atlas, sequential lymph-node-metastasis spatial record, Oprm1-A118G opioid-dependence study, the lung and colorectal CosMx resources, the post-CAR-T marrow spatial atlas, the HNSCC dependency map and the 3D-chromatin-GWAS bundle) has topped every scan since early October - so the actionable harvest again came from the score-7, score-6 and score-4 bands. The novelty filter was applied at two levels: an archive-wide accession check (git log --all -S <GSE> -- src/app/digest/page.tsx returned empty for GSE352985, GSE280374 and GSE336119) and a subject-level keyword-neighbourhood cross-check that confirmed the biological SUBJECTS of all three signals - succinate-mediated suppression of AKT1-overactivation-induced senescence in human colorectal cancer, CD40-agonist-rewired myeloid-T cell interactome hubs in checkpoint-blockade-resistant tumours, and 11beta-HSD2-driven mineralocorticoid-receptor activation in an ageing dental-pulp fibrotic niche - have never been featured under any accession in any prior digest commit. All three records were verified against their live NCBI GEO esummary entries rather than by title matching alone. Signal 1 is GSE352985 (Homo sapiens, n=6, pdat 2026/11/05, raw XLSX, score 6): the depositor summary states a clean, druggable causal chain - succinate suppresses AKT-overactivation-induced cellular senescence and thereby promotes tumour immune evasion; targeting oxoglutarate dehydrogenase reduces succinate production, triggers tumour cellular senescence and enhances antitumour immunity; mechanistically, succinate weakens the interaction between AKT1 and ERK2, lowering ERK2-mediated phosphorylation of AKT1 at Ser473, and this attenuation of AKT overactivation prevents senescence induction; notably OGDH is downregulated in senescent CRC cells, reducing succinate levels - i.e. the enzyme and its product are reciprocally locked with the senescence state itself. Signal 2 is GSE280374 (Mus musculus, n=6, pdat 2026/11/05, raw H5 + MTX + TSV, score 7): the study develops a computational approach to analyse scRNA-seq-derived, single-cell-resolved cell-cell interactomes that manages heterogeneity within cell types, applies it across tumour models to determine how agonistic CD40 alters immune-cell crosstalk alone and in combination with immune checkpoint blockade, and reports that CD40ag improves ICB responses by simultaneously targeting immunostimulatory and immunosuppressive macrophage subsets that communicate with T cells - with the subsets validated spatially by immunofluorescence and spatial transcriptomics, and CD40ag plus ICB establishing coordinated myeloid-T cell interaction hubs critical for re-establishing antitumour immunity. Signal 3 is GSE336119 (Mus musculus, n=2, pdat 2026/11/04, raw CSV + JPG + JSON + MTX + PNG + TSV, score 4): using the continuously growing mouse incisor, the authors integrate scRNA-seq, spatial transcriptomics, lineage tracing and functional assays, identify a Lypd1+ fibroblast progenitor population vulnerable to age-associated dysfunction, trace it to the Sfrp2hi stem-cell pool, and show that early ageing preferentially affects the Lypd1+ progenitors rather than the stem cells, promoting fibrotic conversion through aberrant upregulation of 11beta-HSD2, which enhances aldosterone-mediated mineralocorticoid-receptor activation; ageing also accumulates Ccl4+ macrophages establishing a pro-inflammatory niche in which macrophage-derived PDGFB induces 11beta-HSD2 via P38 MAPK signalling, and in vivo inhibition of the PDGF/P38/11beta-HSD2 axis attenuated age-related pulp fibrosis. The unifying thesis of the day is that the therapeutic lever sits one step above the transcript list: a metabolite-producing enzyme (OGDH), a receptor-ligand axis (CD40 agonism with checkpoint blockade) and a steroid-metabolising enzyme (11beta-HSD2 under mineralocorticoid-receptor control) each convert a measurable metabolic or contact state into a downstream transcriptional programme, and each comes with an already-demonstrated blockade. A second thesis worth carrying is that all three signals are immunologically coupled to senescence and repair state: senescence and its SASP shape antitumour immunity, myeloid-T cell contact geometry determines checkpoint-blockade response, and an ageing niche determines whether repair becomes fibrosis. A process note carried forward rather than patched silently: the score-9 band has now been saturated for twelve consecutive cycles and the highest-value single signal today scored only 4, which again shows that a flat per-record scorer weighting raw-file availability and licence cleanliness over mechanistic specificity systematically delays datasets like the 11beta-HSD2 fibrosis dataset - a mechanism-specificity component in the rubric would surface this material days earlier. Two runner-up signals worth pre-loading: GSE352580 (score 6, n=4) RNA-seq of HGC27 gastric cancer cells with LXRa overexpression induced by GW3965, and GSE349636 (score 4, n=27) Deanr1 regulation of glucose-stimulated insulin secretion and F-actin remodelling in pancreatic beta cells.",
